  "prefLabel": "Puc 2502.10 Class IV source",
  "priorExpiration": "2008-05-25",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Puc 2502.10 “Class IV source” means a hydroelectric generation facility that began operation prior to January 1, 2006, that has a gross nameplate capacity of 5 megawatts or less, and that meets the requirements of RSA 362-F:4, IV.\n\nSource. #9037, INTERIM, eff 11-27-07, EXPIRED: 5-25-08\n\nNew. #9169, eff 6-3-08; ss by #10741, eff 12-5-14 (from Puc 2502.10); ss by #12473, eff 2-1-18 (formerly Puc 2502.09)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/puc2500.html"
